section-number">5.2.5.1</span> Event Type</h4>
            <p><strong>Element name:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventType">lido:eventType</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Event Type indicates the kind of
            an event, whether it is, e.g., the production, acquisition,
            or use of an object in its lifecycle. Terms for these types
            are provided by the LIDO Terminology or by application
            profiles. For related events, and events as subjects of a
            work, the term for Event Type should be drawn from external
            authorities.</p>
            <p>This element is required if &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#event">lido:event</a>&gt;
            is set.</p>
            <p>Terms for Event Type in the object’s lifecycle (&lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventSet">lido:eventSet</a>&gt;)
            are provided by the LIDO <a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/eventType">Event
            Type Vocabulary</a>. If terms of the Event Type Terminology
            are not sufficient for a specific use case concerning the
            object’s lifecycle, compatible vocabulary recommendations
            may be provided within an application profile. Such
            recommendations should ideally extend the LIDO Event Type
            vocabulary.</p>
            <p>Terms for &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#relatedEvent">lido:relatedEvent</a>&gt;
            and &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#subjectEvent">lido:subjectEvent</a>&gt;
            should be drawn from external authorities. For suggestions
            see the LIDO <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/documents/terminology-recommendation.html#subjectEvent">Terminology
            Recommendation</a>.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following example describes
            the production of the <em>Mona Lisa</em> as the most notable
            event. The Event Type is indexed with the concept “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00007">Production</a>”
            from the LIDO Terminology. The mapping relation to the AAT
            descriptor is provided by the LIDO Term.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p><strong>Event:</strong> Painted by Leonardo da Vinci,
            probably between 1503/1519<br /> <strong>Event
            Type:</strong> Production
            <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong> Preferred</p>
            </blockquote>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb30"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb30-1"><a href="#cb30-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:eventSet</span></span>
<span id="cb30-2"><a href="#cb30-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:sortorder=</span><span class="st">&quot;2&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb30-3"><a href="#cb30-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">    lido:mostNotableEvent=</span><span class="st">&quot;1&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-4"><a href="#cb30-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:displayEvent</span></span>
<span id="cb30-5"><a href="#cb30-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-6"><a href="#cb30-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        Painted by Leonardo da Vinci, probably between 1503/1519</span>
<span id="cb30-7"><a href="#cb30-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:displayEvent</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-8"><a href="#cb30-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:event</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-9"><a href="#cb30-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:eventType</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-10"><a href="#cb30-10" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span></span>
<span id="cb30-11"><a href="#cb30-11" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                rdf:about=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00007&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-12"><a href="#cb30-12" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                &lt;<span class="kw">skos:prefLabel</span></span>
<span id="cb30-13"><a href="#cb30-13" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                    xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-14"><a href="#cb30-14" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                    Production</span>
<span id="cb30-15"><a href="#cb30-15" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                &lt;/<span class="kw">skos:prefLabel</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-16"><a href="#cb30-16" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;/<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-17"><a href="#cb30-17" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:eventType</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-18"><a href="#cb30-18" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:event</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb30-19"><a href="#cb30-19" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:eventSet</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h4 data-number="5.2.5.2" id="event-actor"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.2.5.2</span> Event
            Actor</h4>
            <p><strong>Element name:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventActor">lido:eventActor</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Event Actor contains information
            about the person or organization involved in the event in
            focus, including identifying data, names, roles, and
            possibly biographical details.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following example describes
            Leonardo da Vinci in the role of painter. The reference to
            the painting of the <em>Mona Lisa</em> is provided by the
            parent element &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventSet">lido:eventSet</a>&gt;
            with the Event Type “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00007">Production</a>”.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p><strong>Actor:</strong> Painter: Leonardo da Vinci
            (1452–1519)<br /> <strong>Name Actor:</strong> Leonardo, da
            Vinci <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong> Preferred •
            Leonardo da Vinci <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong>
            Display<br /> <strong>Role Actor:</strong> painter
            <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong> Display</p>
            </blockquote>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb31"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb31-1"><a href="#cb31-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:eventActor</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb31-2"><a href="#cb31-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:displayActorInRole</span></span>
<span id="cb31-3"><a href="#cb31-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb31-4"><a href="#cb31-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        Painter: Leonardo da Vinci (1452–1519)</span>
<span id="cb31-5"><a href="#cb31-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:displayActorInRole</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb31-6"><a href="#cb31-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:actorInRole</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb31-7"><a href="#cb31-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>       